hi I'm Evan Carmichael and today I have  a special video for you in collaboration  with Success expert and best-selling  author Brian Tracy today I'm going to  talk about the five characteristics that  set successful entrepreneurs apart once  you're done watching this video make  sure to head over to Brian's channel to  find out his take on the five success  characteristics that every entrepreneur  needs to have the link to his channel  will be in the description below the  first trait of all successful  entrepreneurs is that they are  self-aware they know who they are they  know what they stand for they know what  they want to accomplish they have a very  strong sense of self I believe that  every person has one word that defines  them that is their core value that they  can build their business around for me  it's belief so all of my videos my  business the content I create is all  about belief  I strongly encourage entrepreneurs to  find out what they stand for and use  that as the lens to make your decisions  once you know who you are and what you  stand for it's way easier to make every  single business decision that you need  to make from hiring to product selection  to raising capital everything becomes  easier once you know who you are and  what you stand for  the second trait of successful  entrepreneurs is that they followed  their passion if you look at successful  famous entrepreneurs the most common  piece of advice that you hear over and  over and over and over again is that  they followed their passion passion  passion passion passion passion passion  I should because starting the business  is hard and it's one of the hardest  things that you will ever do in your  life and you need to go through an  insane number of trials and tribulations  running the business will test you and  push you so hard and the only thing that  keeps you going when everybody around  you might be telling you to quit with a  logical safe smart thing to do to quit  the only thing that keeps you going is  the passion that you have for what you  do you have to be crazy and love with  the product or service that you're  creating and if you're not to continue  to explore until you find the thing that  makes you come alive  the third trade is that successful  entrepreneurs see failure as feedback  people who are afraid of failure people  who see failure as permanent and that  they cannot achieve success after the  first failure they never become  successful entrepreneurs the successful  entrepreneurs are the people who  understand that you will fail your way  to success you will fail fail fail fail  fail and then you'll succeed and if you  look at every successful entrepreneur  and you look at how they started they  made a number of critical failures but  they didn't let that stop them they  didn't let that be terminal they didn't  let that be the end of their business  they kept going through those failures  the key is to learn from every failure  if you've learned from the failure then  it's not a failure the only failure is  in not learning from your mistakes  the fourth trait is to model success  understand that whatever problem you're  going through right now someone has  already solved it from acquiring  customers to bring it on partners to get  it into the media to build successful  products whatever it is it's already  been solved by people and the  entrepreneurs who just try to cope with  every single new idea themselves they  often struggle to be successful where  the really successful ones are the ones  who understand that I can model the  success of others that success leaves  clues that by finding out how Bill Gates  became such a successful entrepreneur or  modeling Brian Tracy or modeling Steve  Jobs or modeling people who have already  achieved a lot of success that leaves  clues for you to be able to leave your  own mark on the world and so successful  entrepreneurs are the ones who model  success that has come before them and  then build upon it  and the fifth trait is to create a great  environment it's really hard to do great  things when you are not surrounded by  greatness everything from your habits to  your routine to what's on the wall to  the need that you listen to to the  people that you surround yourself with  your environment either holds you where  you are or encourages you to grow and to  be something amazing and so you have  control over that too many people are  very reactionary and just fall into  their daily routine by accident where if  you plan for greatness if you surround  yourself with greatness every single day  you create that great environment then  you're much more likely to do great  things so those are my top five traits  that every successful entrepreneur must  have I'd encourage you to check out  brian tracy best-selling author and  success expert he made a video on his  channel talking about the same topic  that I'll link up in the description  below and right here on the video now  I'm curious to hear from you what do you  think are the traits that every  successful entrepreneur must have leave  it in the comments below and I'm gonna  join in the discussion thank you so much  for watching  continue to believe and I'll see you  soon
 

